// Instants, timestamps and `Duration` interop — the PLACEHOLDER (0.0.1 P-7).
//
// EMPTY ON PURPOSE: see `../core/core.npk` for why a placeholder exists at all.
// It is REPLACED at the cycle below, never deleted.
//
// WHAT FILLS IT: `Instant` with its clock tag, `Timestamp` with its
// normalisation invariant, the `Duration` constructors `ntime` adds,
// `timestamp_since` with its ±292-year refusal, and `timestamp_until` in
// calendar units. Governed by `meta/specs/SPAN_MODEL.md`.
// WHEN: cycle 0.2 (`meta/roadmap/0.2/README.md`).
//
// WHAT IT MAY IMPORT: `cal` and `core` (`BUILD.md` B-17).
//
// WHAT IT MUST NOT DECLARE: a `Duration` (TM-004). The prelude's is the
// ecosystem's one span type; a second would immediately become the type
// everybody converts to and from.
mod:span;
